    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0334" n="292" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg292"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 414.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-05-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 14, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit a copy of a
                    note of Lord Russell to me of the 8th instant, in reply to mine of the 22d
                    ultimo, which was sent to you with my No. 389, of the 24th of April, on the
                    subject of the steamer Sumter. I presume this closes the correspondence.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d199-a1.xml" xpointer="d199-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
